 = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 9} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{9}^{2}} & = \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d9827850-9b38-58c0-a560-bbc82a0bfdd5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d9827850-9b38-58c0-a560-bbc82a0bfdd5" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9827850-9b38-58c0-a560-bbc82a0bfdd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-37bb337e-9900-555f-884a-4f079ca34ab7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce3e7796-3c29-5861-8a8d-521ee069f312" "answer-9286a35c-2dc6-53af-8c6e-4f5e43cb3915" "answer-37bb337e-9900-555f-884a-4f079ca34ab7" "answer-331769fd-392c-5fa7-8159-3a314da12662" "answer-353db5e0-fb0c-5857-a2f5-6090c135c5ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce3e7796-3c29-5861-8a8d-521ee069f312" :answer/id #uuid "ce3e7796-3c29-5861-8a8d-521ee069f312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9286a35c-2dc6-53af-8c6e-4f5e43cb3915" :answer/id #uuid "9286a35c-2dc6-53af-8c6e-4f5e43cb3915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37bb337e-9900-555f-884a-4f079ca34ab7" :answer/id #uuid "37bb337e-9900-555f-884a-4f079ca34ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-331769fd-392c-5fa7-8159-3a314da12662" :answer/id #uuid "331769fd-392c-5fa7-8159-3a314da12662" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-353db5e0-fb0c-5857-a2f5-6090c135c5ff" :answer/id #uuid "353db5e0-fb0c-5857-a2f5-6090c135c5ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078911 :question/problem "Find the value of the expression $\\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times ({3}^{2}-5)÷2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times ({3}^{2}-5)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times (9-5)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{3}\\times (4)÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{8\\times 4÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{32÷2} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{16} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{4}^{2}} & = \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186076244 :answer-field/correct 17592186076248 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c3c665d-7d8f-59dd-ac27-822edd107571" :question/id #uuid "1c3c665d-7d8f-59dd-ac27-822edd107571" :question/math-academy-id "q-69301" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}÷(1-{3}^{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}÷(1-{3}^{2}) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5}÷(1-9) & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5}÷(-8) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{(-8)} & = \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b0387295-9fb7-5920-87f6-eab66a076f57"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0387295-9fb7-5920-87f6-eab66a076f57" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0387295-9fb7-5920-87f6-eab66a076f57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2a791971-c0af-5b44-9234-69c51ab2a6c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2a791971-c0af-5b44-9234-69c51ab2a6c5" "answer-e090c643-e386-5c56-8d35-64ec35e4b767" "answer-a805033e-a7ac-519f-b33f-976141e7d52a" "answer-ba1ccd6c-cca7-5e3e-8208-780deb7db979" "answer-6ede240d-6358-55b6-9cf4-b903ea2291a3"]