nsure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ea0794d-3afe-5094-adc5-733705a0114e" :answer/id #uuid "7ea0794d-3afe-5094-adc5-733705a0114e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09adec12-840c-52e4-a460-053eee3c485d" :answer/id #uuid "09adec12-840c-52e4-a460-053eee3c485d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4ae171d6-ef6c-513e-bb69-e2d14e0a590f" :question/id #uuid "4ae171d6-ef6c-513e-bb69-e2d14e0a590f" :question/math-academy-id "q-69265" :question/problem "What is the value of $2\\sqrt{(3-6)\\times (1-3)}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{(3-6)\\times (1-3)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{(-3)\\times (-2)} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we approximate the value of the radical using a calculator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & ≈‭‭‭2.449\\,490\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we approximate the value of the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{6} & ≈ \\\\ 2(2.449\\,490) & ≈ \\\\ 4.898\\,98 & ≈ \\\\ 4.899\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-caa3dfcf-a676-51da-a5bf-f83fd246ee39"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-caa3dfcf-a676-51da-a5bf-f83fd246ee39" :answer-field/id #uuid "caa3dfcf-a676-51da-a5bf-f83fd246ee39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4bde511a-ac2b-53f9-9089-b2a6e07cae57" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4350ad3f-e88d-53a1-8fb1-12f2d61c6199" "answer-1c288773-6605-52e2-ac4b-f6bd250