t "answer-9d6e43d3-232d-52f2-810c-0a514fc301c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b2e2ed4-8577-5b51-bcd5-fe6c9eb1aee1" "answer-85da8dec-b7f8-5bc2-a8cc-1e1fb0c3211c" "answer-e80f03a3-463c-5484-906b-72bc65a58138" "answer-94a416e6-2fec-5d8c-84ab-cd7d3ed32ea8" "answer-9d6e43d3-232d-52f2-810c-0a514fc301c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b2e2ed4-8577-5b51-bcd5-fe6c9eb1aee1" :answer/id #uuid "5b2e2ed4-8577-5b51-bcd5-fe6c9eb1aee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4-x)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85da8dec-b7f8-5bc2-a8cc-1e1fb0c3211c" :answer/id #uuid "85da8dec-b7f8-5bc2-a8cc-1e1fb0c3211c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(8-x)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e80f03a3-463c-5484-906b-72bc65a58138" :answer/id #uuid "e80f03a3-463c-5484-906b-72bc65a58138" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+16)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94a416e6-2fec-5d8c-84ab-cd7d3ed32ea8" :answer/id #uuid "94a416e6-2fec-5d8c-84ab-cd7d3ed32ea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d6e43d3-232d-52f2-810c-0a514fc301c4" :answer/id #uuid "9d6e43d3-232d-52f2-810c-0a514fc301c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+8)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-380d2267-0a37-5388-bacc-f5df7afa8e5c" :question/id #uuid "380d2267-0a37-5388-bacc-f5df7afa8e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-2687" :question/problem "Factor the expression ${n}^{2}-8n+16.$" :question/worked-solution "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{n}^{2}-2an+{a}^{2}=(n-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{n}^{2}-8n+16.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-8n+{4}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-2\\cdot 4n+{4}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-4)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-60e32385-f789-5db5-9751-6f5995c30fbf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-60e32385-f789-5db5-9751-6f5995c30fbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "60e32385-f789-5db5-9751-6f5995c30fbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89cab026-bd1e-5e16-ba6d-f1664b8986a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-40ce3321-cec7-5aaa-b54a-09de1c3c1af9" "answer-e9376aa9-6236-5424-883c-0812e7f547c9" "answer-62cc44c6-12eb-55b8-a7d4-1042cc8714cc" "answer-89cab026-bd1e-5e16-ba6d-f1664b8986a5" "answer-8fe97e30-2a6b-5f25-9426-d0aa4ba82142"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40ce3321-cec7-5aaa-b54a-09de1c3c1af9" :answer/id #uuid "40ce3321-cec7-5aaa-b54a-09de1c3c1af9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n+4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9376aa9-6236-5424-883c-0812e7f547c9" :answer/id #uuid "e9376aa9-6236-5424-883c-0812e7f547c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n+8)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62cc44c6-12eb-55b8-a7d4-1042cc8714cc" :answer/id #uuid "62cc44c6-12eb-55b8-a7d4-1042cc8714cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n-2)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89cab026-bd1e-5e16-ba6d-f1664b8986a5" :answer/id #uuid "89cab026-bd1e-5e16-ba6d-f1664b8986a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n-4)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fe97e30-2a6b-5f25-9426-d0aa4ba82142" :answer/id #uuid "8fe97e30-2a6b-5f25-9426-d0aa4ba82142" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(n-8)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-94bbfbab-f0f9-56d8-b645-4168ecf299d7" :question/id #uuid "94bbfbab-f0f9-56d8-b645-4168ecf299d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-111614" :question/problem "Factor $-24f+144+{f}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{f}^{2}-2af+{a}^{2}=(f-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n-24f+144+{f}^{2}={f}^{2}-24f+144\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{2}-24f+{12}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{2}-2\\cdot 12f+{12}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=12.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f-12)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3b60d8d3-458f-57a9-a05e-b1eed04df77d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b60d8d3-458f-57a9-a05e-b1eed04df77d" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b60d8d3-458f-57a9-a05e-b1eed04df77d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-71b0d67f-b692-5b74-8be6-cd36bd3a3167" :answer-field/choices ["answer-71b0d67f-b692-5b74-8be6-cd36bd3a3167" "answer-27e0b737-f825-5a71-b6f8-35f4cbcbf6ef" "answer-7d4790ae-db54-5599-899a-42565aec55b3" "answer-74fa1824-5bac-55bf-81f2-628a0fda9417" "answer-35b4ee71-4ad1-54b2-830a-99e9af4036c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71b0d67f-b692-5b74-8be6-cd36bd3a3167" :answer/id #uuid "71b0d67f-b692-5b74-8be6-cd36bd3a3167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(f-12)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27e0b737-f825-5a71-b6f8-35f4cbcbf6ef" :answer/id #uuid "27e0b737-f825-5a71-b6f8-35f4cbcbf6ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(f-20)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d4790ae-db54-5599-899a-42565aec55b3" :answer/id #uuid "7d4790ae-db54-5599-899a-42565aec55b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(f-24)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74fa1824-5bac-55bf-81f2-628a0fda9417" :answer/id #uuid "74fa1824-5bac-55bf-81f2-628a0fda9417" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(f-6)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35b4ee71-4ad1-54b2-830a-99e9af4036c1" :answer/id #uuid "35b4ee71-4ad1-54b2-830a-99e9af4036c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(f-9)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f18cf588-d703-5104-bc39-415b94a76959" :question/id #uuid "f18cf588-d703-5104-bc39-415b94a76959" :question/math-academy-id "q-31845" :question/problem "${x}^{2}+100-20x$ is equivalent to" :question/worked-solution "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2ax+{a}^{2}=(x-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+100-20x={x}^{2}-20x+100.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-20x+{10}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 10x+{10}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=10.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-10)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b0dc3f1-b5b1-5200-a64b-568ebc36fda2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b0dc3f1-b5b1-5200-a64b-568ebc36fda2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b0dc3f1-b5b1-5200-a64b-568ebc36fda2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-997f08c7-8c76-5407-ad33-a50dbbf851cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b6c3f97e-3782-58c0-ad2f-f95a54618783" "answer-7ed35112-5230-5213-899f-b5c028d022e9" "answer-997f08c7-8c76-5407-ad33-a50dbbf851cb" "answer-33ad99fc-1f72-5f18-91bc-a87ebce61eca" "answer-8509ee32-0054-5a82-9df9-6ca422de6360"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6c3f97e-3782-58c0-ad2f-f95a54618783" :answer/id #uuid "b6c3f97e-3782-58c0-ad2f-f95a54618783" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+10)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ed35112-5230-5213-899f-b5c028d022e9" :answer/id #uuid "7ed35112-5230-5213-899f-b5c028d022e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-997f08c7-8c76-5407-ad33-a50dbbf851cb" :answer/id #uuid "997f08c7-8c76-5407-ad33-a50dbbf851cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-10)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33ad99fc-1f72-5f18-91bc-a87ebce61eca" :answer/id #uuid "33ad99fc-1f72-5f18-91bc-a87ebce61eca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-20)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8509ee32-0054-5a82-9df9-6ca422de6360" :answer/id #uuid "8509ee32-0054-5a82-9df9-6ca422de6360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3ab2e3ce-42ef-5550-a256-e8688e7ed48b" :question/id #uuid "3ab2e3ce-42ef-5550-a256-e8688e7ed48b" :question/math-academy-id "q-111618" :question/problem "Factor the expression ${n}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}n+\\frac{25}{16}.$" :question/worked-solution "The \"square of a sum\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{n}^{2}+2an+{a}^{2}=(n+a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{n}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}n+\\frac{25}{16}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}n+{(\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}n+{(\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of sum formula with $a=\\frac{5}{4}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(n+\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6650d077-6bfe-5e18-8868-b906e55313a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6650d077-6bfe-5e18-8868-b906e55313a6" :answer-field/id #uuid "6650d077-6bfe-5e18-8868-b906e55313a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d534e72-0930-51b5-a1d0-f3aa1de73e46" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12f1b3aa-ebc1-51c1-8273-c4b915d8ecf4" "answer-898c7c3f-dd8f-5773-abc2-e29cff260011" "answer-7e777da0-d7e0-58cc-ba96-49a1a74e9598" "answer-9d033726-a4f4-50d9-b131-7a5467c7dc90" "answer-3d534e72-0930-51b5-a1d0-f3aa1de73e46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12f1b3aa-ebc1-51c1-8273-c4b915d8ecf4" :answer/id #uuid "12f1b3aa-ebc1-51c1-8273-c4b915d8ecf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{25}{16})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-898c7c3f-dd8f-5773-abc2-e29cff260011" :answer/id #uuid "898c7c3f-dd8f-5773-abc2-e29cff260011" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{25}{4})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e777da0-d7e0-58cc-ba96-49a1a74e9598" :answer/id #uuid "7e777da0-d7e0-58cc-ba96-49a1a74e9598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{5}{16})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d033726-a4f4-50d9-b131-7a5467c7dc90" :answer/id #uuid "9d033726-a4f4-50d9-b131-7a5467c7dc90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d534e72-0930-51b5-a1d0-f3aa1de73e46" :answer/id #uuid "3d534e72-0930-51b5-a1d0-f3aa1de73e46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-33ad6f1c-10b4-54e8-b066-192c2a7ae636" :question/id #uuid "33ad6f1c-10b4-54e8-b066-192c2a7ae636" :question/math-academy-id "q-111620" :question/problem "Factor ${p}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}p+\\frac{9}{16}.$" :question/worked-solution "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{p}^{2}-2ap+{a}^{2}=(p-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{p}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}p+\\frac{9}{16}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}p+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}p+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=\\frac{3}{4}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(p-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68e62d53-fe58-5a69-aba9-9a9c52260323"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68e62d53-fe58-5a69-aba9-9a9c52260323" :answer-field/id #uuid "68e62d53-fe58-5a69-aba9-9a9c52260323" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4e12cabb-23ac-5417-9a7a-ef3c27b9cbcc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6481951b-42c4-5e4f-90f7-2774c2f713bb" "answer-8350d09e-a155-59ee-9cf8-3c2e7a019dc2" "answer-4e12cabb-23ac-5417-9a7a-ef3c27b9cbcc" "answer-25237418-8897-5984-a318-b9d6acfd3dbf" "answer-336a6d96-d960-535c-95fb-75d4c09869fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6481951b-42c4-5e4f-90f7-2774c2f713bb" :answer/id #uuid "6481951b-42c4-5e4f-90f7-2774c2f713bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(p-\\frac{3}{16})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8350d09e-a155-59ee-9cf8-3c2e7a019dc2" :answer/id #uuid "8350d09e-a155-59ee-9cf8-3c2e7a019dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(p-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e12cabb-23ac-5417-9a7a-ef3c27b9cbcc" :answer/id #uuid "4e12cabb-23ac-5417-9a7a-ef3c27b9cbcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(p-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25237418-8897-5984-a318-b9d6acfd3dbf" :answer/id #uuid "25237418-8897-5984-a318-b9d6acfd3dbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(p-\\frac{9}{16})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-336a6d96-d960-535c-95fb-75d4c09869fb" :answer/id #uuid "336a6d96-d960-535c-95fb-75d4c09869fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(p-\\frac{9}{4})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065341 :tutorial/content "A **perfect square trinomial** is a three-term expression that is the result of squaring a binomial.\n\nFor example, the expression\n\n$$\nx^2 + 6x + 9\n$$\n\nis a perfect square trinomial because it is the result of squaring the binomial $(x+3)$, as shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x+9 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo factor a perfect square trinomial, we have to figure out what binomial it is the square of. We can often do this by relating the perfect square trinomial to the **square of a sum**:\n\n$$\nx^2 + {\\color{red}2}  {\\color{blue}a}x + {\\color{blue}a}^2 = (x + {\\color{blue}a})^2\n$$\n\n \n\nTo illustrate, let's factor the expression $x^2+6x+9$ using the square of sum formula. We perform the following steps:\n\n1\\. Write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n3\\. Factor the trinomial using the \"square of a sum formula\". In this case, we have ${\\color{blue}{a}}={\\color{blue}{3}}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nThis method works *only* when the trinomial is a perfect square! It will *not* work for every trinomial. We will learn more general methods in the future." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065345 :tutorial/content "Other perfect square trinomials can be factored as the **square of a difference**:\n\n$$\nx^2 - {\\color{red}2}  {\\color{blue}a}x  + {\\color{blue}a}^2 = (x - {\\color{blue}a})^2\n$$\n\n \n\nTo illustrate, let's factor the expression $x^2-10x+25$ using the square of difference formula. We perform the following steps:\n\n1\\. Write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x+{5}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n3\\. Factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula. In this case, we have ${\\color{blue}{a}}={\\color{blue}{5}},$ and we get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n  $$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064441 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068701 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-86c185f8-7069-5803-a8a3-6aebf9cf8dbc" "question-a662c339-4277-548c-aaa6-345c7b02ceaa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068486 :question/problem "If $g(x) = (x-4)^2+3(5-x)$, calculate $g(2).$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=2$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tg(x) &= (x-4)^2+3(5-x) \\[5pt]\n\t\tg(2) &= (2-4)^2+3(5-2) \\[5pt]\n\t\t      &= (-2)^2+3(3) \\[5pt]\n\t\t      &= 4 + 9 \\[5pt]\n\t\t      &= 13\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068702 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9ddffbc5-a8dd-53fa-a3bc-4cc663a782e3" "question-377f9da3-7e91-540b-b15e-84984d6004ce"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068487 :question/problem "Evaluate $f(4,-1)$ if $f(x,y)= 3\\cdot 2^{x+3y}.$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=4$ and $y=-1$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =3\\cdot {2}^{x+3y} \\\\ f(4,-1) & =3\\cdot {2}^{4+3(-1)} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{4-3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {2}^{1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-86c185f8-7069-5803-a8a3-6aebf9cf8dbc" :question/id #uuid "86c185f8-7069-5803-a8a3-6aebf9cf8dbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-35796" :question/problem "Find the value of $f(t)=(t+1)^{2}-2(t+1)$ at $t=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $t=-2$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(t+1)^{2}-2(t+1) \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2+1)^{2}-2(-2+1) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-2(-1) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f16ab47-5e41-5f62-8b8a-f141f8ee7ffc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f16ab47-5e41-5f62-8b8a-f141f8ee7ffc" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f16ab47-5e41-5f62-8b8a-f141f8ee7ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8d159bd3-ad14-53c2-a7b8-ac88014f10b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e2cc33ad-9851-56cb-8073-0d7b5da205d9" "answer-c773536d-4803-5b61-b3eb-4cda7f75454f" "answer-4ca75c3d-4868-5830-9738-11577069a7a9" "answer-8d159bd3-ad14-53c2-a7b8-ac88014f10b7" "answer-5bdec0d5-25bb-599c-bb88-de95a33396e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2cc33ad-9851-56cb-8073-0d7b5da205d9" :answer/id #uuid "e2cc33ad-9851-56cb-8073-0d7b5da205d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c773536d-4803-5b61-b3eb-4cda7f75454f" :answer/id #uuid "c773536d-4803-5b61-b3eb-4cda7f75454f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ca75c3d-4868-5830-9738-11577069a7a9" :answer/id #uuid "4ca75c3d-4868-5830-9738-11577069a7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d159bd3-ad14-53c2-a7b8-ac88014f10b7" :answer/id #uuid "8d159bd3-ad14-53c2-a7b8-ac88014f10b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bdec0d5-25bb-599c-bb88-de95a33396e1" :answer/id #uuid "5bdec0d5-25bb-599c-bb88-de95a33396e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a662c339-4277-548c-aaa6-345c7b02ceaa" :question/id #uuid "a662c339-4277-548c-aaa6-345c7b02ceaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-31666" :question/problem "Evaluate $g(2),$ if $g(x)=(x-3)(x+4)(x-7).$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=2$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =(x-3)(x+4)(x-7) \\\\ g(2) & =(2-3)(2+4)(2-7) \\\\  & =(-1)(6)(-5) \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9efe11b6-9e5a-5718-855d-0ceb47e59c9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9efe11b6-9e5a-5718-855d-0ceb47e59c9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9efe11b6-9e5a-5718-855d-0ceb47e59c9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b857a0f1-501b-5f87-851a-332c8930b6b5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9deb7ae3-7740-5a1f-837e-aa18418ee2b6" "answer-1c65c371-84c2-5336-a5ba-b786e1391ad7" "answer-21a4b4b6-d1ed-5313-8755-aabe9512feb5" "answer-b857a0f1-501b-5f87-851a-332c8930b6b5" "answer-43ed415e-f5fe-55ff-8e1c-c259e3c52856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9deb7ae3-7740-5a1f-837e-aa18418ee2b6" :answer/id #uuid "9deb7ae3-7740-5a1f-837e-aa18418ee2b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(2)=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c65c371-84c2-5336-a5ba-b786e1391ad7" :answer/id #uuid "1c65c371-84c2-5336-a5ba-b786e1391ad7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(2)=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21a4b4b6-d1ed-5313-8755-aabe9512feb5" :answer/id #uuid "21a4b4b6-d1ed-5313-8755-aabe9512feb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(2)=20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b857a0f1-501b-5f87-851a-332c8930b6b5" :answer/id #uuid "b857a0f1-501b-5f87-851a-332c8930b6b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(2)=30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43ed415e-f5fe-55ff-8e1c-c259e3c52856" :answer/id #uuid "43ed415e-f5fe-55ff-8e1c-c259e3c52856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(2)=32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9ddffbc5-a8dd-53fa-a3bc-4cc663a782e3" :question/id #uuid "9ddffbc5-a8dd-53fa-a3bc-4cc663a782e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130589" :question/problem "Evaluate $f(-3,0)$ if $f(x,y)={5}^{x+4}+x\\cdot {2}^{y+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=-3$ and $y=0$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={5}^{x+4}+x\\cdot {2}^{y+1} \\\\ f(-3,0) & ={5}^{-3+4}+(-3)\\cdot {2}^{0+1} \\\\  & ={5}^{1}+(-3)\\cdot {2}^{1} \\\\  & ={5}^{1}-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5-6 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d6bf835a-c22c-5719-9a97-7f315f41a30c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d6bf835a-c22c-5719-9a97-7f315f41a30c" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6bf835a-c22c-5719-9a97-7f315f41a30c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6da051be-bc81-55c6-82ce-1cbc6e6910b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6da051be-bc81-55c6-82ce-1cbc6e6910b0" "answer-b46e3c41-c7cb-5a9e-b9fa-969fa30804dd" "answer-9aec1c44-03f2-54d9-ba49-2cf0c1e42dd3" "answer-a331c3e3-47a9-5909-84c0-abb30861da31" "answer-111ff245-85aa-568e-aeb5-1f58b333c4bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6da051be-bc81-55c6-82ce-1cbc6e6910b0" :answer/id #uuid "6da051be-bc81-55c6-82ce-1cbc6e6910b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b46e3c41-c7cb-5a9e-b9fa-969fa30804dd" :answer/id #uuid "b46e3c41-c7cb-5a9e-b9fa-969fa30804dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9aec1c44-03f2-54d9-ba49-2cf0c1e42dd3" :answer/id #uuid "9aec1c44-03f2-54d9-ba49-2cf0c1e42dd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a331c3e3-47a9-5909-84c0-abb30861da31" :answer/id #uuid "a331c3e3-47a9-5909-84c0-abb30861da31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-111ff245-85aa-568e-aeb5-1f58b333c4bc" :answer/id #uuid "111ff245-85aa-568e-aeb5-1f58b333c4bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-377f9da3-7e91-540b-b15e-84984d6004ce" :question/id #uuid "377f9da3-7e91-540b-b15e-84984d6004ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-214851" :question/problem "If $g(u,v)=3\\cdot {5}^{2u-3v}-2u,$ then $g(5,3)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $u=5$ and $v=3$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(u,v) & =3\\cdot {5}^{2u-3v}-2u \\\\ g(5,3) & =3\\cdot {5}^{2(5)-3(3)}-2(5) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {5}^{10-9}-10 \\\\  & =3\\cdot {5}^{1}-10 \\\\  & =15-10 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74583649-f1a5-51a3-a457-5e1abe4ddf06"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74583649-f1a5-51a3-a457-5e1abe4ddf06" :answer-field/id #uuid "74583649-f1a5-51a3-a457-5e1abe4ddf06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-41647c32-39d8-5520-9ac1-9758281e2a40" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41647c32-39d8-5520-9ac1-9758281e2a40"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41647c32-39d8-5520-9ac1-9758281e2a40" :answer/id #uuid "41647c32-39d8-5520-9ac1-9758281e2a40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069116 :question/problem "If $g(a,b)=(a-b)({a}^{2}-{b}^{2}),$ then $g(2,-2)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $a=2$ and $b=-2$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(a,b) & =(a-b)({a}^{2}-{b}^{2}) \\\\ g(2,-2) & =((2)-(-2))((2)^{2}-(-2)^{2}) \\\\  & =(2+2)(4-4) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186066112 :answer-field/correct "answer-d8d28ec1-8bca-5b66-95e1-e3b9c1576a50" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8d28ec1-8bca-5b66-95e1-e3b9c1576a50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8d28ec1-8bca-5b66-95e1-e3b9c1576a50" :answer/id #uuid "d8d28ec1-8bca-5b66-95e1-e3b9c1576a50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070022 :tutorial/content "A **function** is a rule that takes a number as **input** and then **outputs** another number.\n\nFor instance, let's look at the following function: \n\n$$\nf(x) = 3x+1\n$$\n\nIn this example,\n\n- $f$ is the **name** of the function,\n\n- the number $x$ is the **input**,\n\n- the number $3x+1$ is the **output**.\n\nIf we **substitute** a number into our function in place of $x$, we get another number as output. \n\nFor example, by substituting $x={\\color{blue}{2}},$ we get\n\n$$\nf({\\color{blue}{2}}) = 3\\cdot {\\color{blue}{2}}+1 = 7.\n$$\n\nSo, the input $x={\\color{blue}{2}}$ results in an output of $7.$\n\nWe can substitute any number we like into this function! For example, if we substitute $x={\\color{red}{-2}},$ we get\n\n$$\nf({\\color{red}{-2}}) = 3\\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}})+1 = -5.\n$$\n\nSo, the input $x={\\color{red}{-2}}$ results in an output of $-5.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070023 :tutorial/content "Functions with more than one input are called **multivariable functions**. \n\nFor example, the multivariable function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x-y\n$$\n\ntakes in two numbers, $x$ and $y$, and returns their difference. \n\nFor multivariable functions, the order of the inputs matters. For example, if we substitute $x={\\color{blue}{3}}$ and $y={\\color{red}{2}},$ we get\n\n$$\nf({\\color{blue}{3}},{\\color{red}{2}}) = {\\color{blue}{3}}-{\\color{red}{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nwhereas if we substitute $x={\\color{red}{2}}$ and $y={\\color{blue}{3}},$ we get a different output:\n\n$$\nf({\\color{red}{2}},{\\color{blue}{3}})={\\color{red}{2}}-{\\color{blue}{3}}=-1\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068995 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176484 :question/problem "What is $(\\sqrt{64})^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The number in the square root is non-negative, so the square and the square root cancel each other out.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n(\\sqrt{64})^{2}=64.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175042 :answer-field/correct 17592186175047 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175917 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ad6df804-3e3c-5d45-acbc-edbd4509746d" "question-da6d460c-dde7-5fc1-ac50-c5ee168f1351"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ad6df804-3e3c-5d45-acbc-edbd4509746d" :question/id #uuid "ad6df804-3e3c-5d45-acbc-edbd4509746d" :question/math-academy-id "q-69750" :question/problem "What is $\\sqrt{{(-36)}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that by definition, the square root is always zero or positive, never negative.\n\nSo, the square root comes out to\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{(-36)^{2}}=\\sqrt{{36}^{2}}=36.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61228407-9b50-5d5e-8859-cbf8ab07e73b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61228407-9b50-5d5e-8859-cbf8ab07e73b" :answer-field/id #uuid "61228407-9b50-5d5e-8859-cbf8ab07e73b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dfb477dd-f26c-5b3f-8833-6f12839a60d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0561decb-7e57-5d8d-98fc-79752f342f51" "answer-445ae046-f9c4-5f28-92c9-c8ffe97025d6" "answer-dfb477dd-f26c-5b3f-8833-6f12839a60d3" "answer-e2a559a8-743c-5e88-8b4d-b691e17f2fef" "answer-e759f29b-0ea4-5a5d-b64b-64a3e53e26b4"] :db/ensure [:a